<title>USA: FDA panel backs new use of Summit eye laser.</title>
<headline>FDA panel backs new use of Summit eye laser.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Food and Drug Administration advisory committee voted unanimously Friday to approve a new procedure to correct severe near-sightedness which uses a laser manufactured by Summit Technology.</p>
<p>The procedure, called laser in-situ keratomileusis (LASIK) and the software to support it was developed by Doctor George Waring of the Emory Vision Correction Center in Atlanta, Ga.</p>
